---
layout: tutorial
title: Configure web platform
description: Add paid app subscription plans to your app with Stripe and Appwrite Functions.
step: 4
---

## Add platform {% #add-platform %}
To showcase the functionality, the template ships with a demo frontend that you can use. To allow this demo, you must add the function's domain as a trusted web app. You can find your function's domain under the function's **Domains** tab.

{% only_dark %}
![Functions domain](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/dark/functions-stripe-domain.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Functions domain](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/functions-stripe-domain.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Head to your project's **Overview** page in the Appwrite Console, and click **Add app** in the **Apps** section. Select **Web** as the platform and **No framework** as the web framework, then click **Continue**.

{% only_dark %}
![Add a platform](/images/docs/quick-starts/dark/add-platform.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Add a platform](/images/docs/quick-starts/add-platform.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Set **Name** to `Subscription demo` and **Hostname** to your function's domain, without `https://`. Click **Register and continue**.

You don't need to follow the remaining setup instructions, so you can click **Done**.

## Update webhook endpoint {% #update-webhook-endpoint %}

Go back to the [Webhooks](https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks) tab in Stripe's Workbench and select the destination you created earlier. Click **Edit destination** and update its **Endpoint URL** to `https://<YOUR_FUNCTION_DOMAIN>/webhook`. For example, `https://subscriptions-with-stripe.fra.appwrite.run/webhook`.

The signing secret stays the same, so you don't need to change the function's variables.
